  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed amendment to the red line boundary requires changes to the operative part of the planning permission, being the site location, which falls outside the provisions of Section 73 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "Insufficient information, in terms of drainage calculations, has been submitted to satisfy the requirements of Condition 12 (sustainable drainage system) of planning permission 17/14450/FUL. The applicant has not provided drainage calculation results which are required to demonstrate that the proposed drainage system can indeed contain up to the 1 in 30 storm event without flooding and that any onsite flooding between the 1 in 30 and the 1 in 100 plus 40% climate change storm event would be safely contained on site. The proposal fails to demonstrate it would not increase flood risk elsewhere, contrary to Policy SI 13 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM4 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
